INSERT INTO public.exam_questions (subject_id,subject_name,year,position,text,options,answer,explanation) VALUES
(5,'Biology','2017',81,'Which of the following is an example of anthropogenic driving factor that contributes to species extinction?','["Earth quack", "Volcanic eruption", "Expansions of agriculture", "Outbreak of wild-fire"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',82,'Which one of the following statements is correct about nervous system? It','["takes air into and out of the body to supply oxygen and remove carbon dioxide.", "uses blood vessels to transport blood around the body through the heart.", "consist of cells that produce and secret chemicals into the blood stream via duct.", "receives and processes sensory information from internal and external parts of the body."]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',83,'What is the best justification for the role of voltage-gated ion channels in nerve impulse transmission? They','["actively respond to membrane potential changes, leading to depolarization.", "block the ions movement across the membrane to sustain neuron.", "allow potassium ions diffuse to the inside of the membrane, forming repolarization.", "produce energy when the sodium ions move to the inside of the axon."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',84,'Which one of the following ions are used to facilitate the release of neurotransmitters to the synaptic cleft before binding to postsynaptic receptor?','["Calcium ions", "Magnesium ions", "Potassium ions", "Sodium ions"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',85,'Find the correct pathway of reflex arc that prevents you from physical damage upon the sudden touching of hot plate.','["Interneuron → receptor → motor neuron → effector", "Sensory neuron → motor neuron → spinal cord → effector", "Sensory neuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → effector", "Interneuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → effector"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',86,'Select the option that contains the correct match of human ear structure and its function.','["Eustachian tube - balancing air pressure of the middle ear and throat", "Semicircular canals - concerned with production of nerve impulse", "Ear ossicles - concerned with the detection of motion", "Cochlea - transmits sound from the incus to the auditory nerve"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',87,'This item is based on the following list of events that happen during hearing. I. Transmission of amplified sound waves to the ear ossicles II. Movement of sensory hair as a result of vibration of the fluid in the cochlea III. Transmission of nerve impulse into the brain and response to the sound stimulus IV. The pinna directs sound waves into the eardrum Based on the above lists, which alternative shows the correct steps of the events of hearing?','["IV → III → II → I", "I → II → III → IV", "I → IV → II → III", "IV → I → II → III"]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',88,'Suppose low metabolic rate, cretinism and retarded mental and physical development are common problems of infants and childhood in a small village. Which condition in the endocrine system results in these problems?','["Extreme hypothyroidism", "Malfunction of adrenal cortex", "Over production of parathyroid hormone", "Lack of adrenalin production"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',89,'If a woman is admitted to hospital for giving birth, which hormone is helping her in the delivery of her baby and releasing of milk?','["Vasopressin", "Aldosterone", "Oxytocin", "Progesterone"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',90,'How ultrafiltration takes place in the human kidney? By','["increasing the concentration of urine in the muscular sac using a collecting duct", "building the pressure of the knot of blood vessels in the Bowman''s capsule", "diffusing of glucose molecules into the first coiled tubule of microvilli", "reabsorbing of water into the blood in the second coiled tubule using ADH"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',91,'Assume a patient with type II diabetes gets advice to practice regular exercise to raise the number of insulin receptors. Then, how does insulin regulate the blood glucose level if it is high in this patient? It stimulates','["glycolysis, which converts glucose into pyruvate.", "glycogenesis, which converts glucose into glycogen.", "lipolysis that converts fatty acid into glucose.", "gluconeogenesis that creates glucose from amino acids."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',92,'Imagine the water content of the blood is low when you take in much salt with your food. What would happen in your kidney to regulate this situation? Osmoreceptor stimulates the','["adrenal gland to release adrenalin that increases conversion of glycogen to glucose in the blood.", "hypothalamus that release aldosterone and sodium ions to reabsorb back into the blood.", "pituitary gland to release ADH to reabsorb water back into the blood.", "ADH to release cortisone that promotes resistance to water stress."]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',93,'Several current studies point out that very large quantity of greenhouse gases have been added into Earth''s atmosphere due to human activities. What would be the most likely responsible gas and its major sources, respectively?','["Methane - aluminum smelting and semiconductor manufacturing", "Carbon dioxide - fossil fuel combustion, deforestation, oil and gas usage", "Sulphur hexafluoride - landfills, rice paddies, digestive tracts of cattle", "Perfluorocarbons - electric transmission, magnesium and aluminum production"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',94,'The effect of increased climate change on agricultural productivity is associated with','["land use change and expansion of monoculture farming that yields high productivity.", "agroforestry system that increases the mixture of multipurpose trees and crops.", "drought that triggers wild fire, which can consume millions of acres of forest.", "reduction of available water that leads to decrease in biological resources."]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',95,'Which one of the following local community practices in Ethiopia is considered as an environmental action that addresses climate change mitigation? Culture of','["respecting humanity that promotes eco-tourism industry", "negotiating mechanism that is led by elders to reduce social unrest", "planting millions of seedlings following the green legacy initiative", "treating different diseases with herbal remedies by traditional healers"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',96,'Which labeled part is responsible for controlling the diameter of the pupil according to the light source?','["I", "II", "III", "IV"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',97,'Consider the following diagram of pyramid of biomass','["The whole organisms at first trophic level is eaten by the organisms above.", "When organisms in stage II eat the producers, most of the producer''s materials are turned into new secondary consumers.", "Much of the biomass from stage II is used by stage III to release energy for living.", "At each stage of trophic level, the amount of biomass, which is passed on, supports a large"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',98,'Consider the following structure of the human heart.','["I", "II", "III", "IV"]'::jsonb,2,'');